  "before": {
    "label": "a banana (potassium-40)",
    "text": "About 0.1 μSv — natural background itself runs 2–3 millisieverts per year worldwide, roughly half of it radon gas."
  },
  "after": {
    "label": "a milligray of internal alpha",
    "text": "Alpha's dense ionisation track does concentrated local harm — roughly twenty times more damaging per gray than gamma inside the body. Radon in poorly ventilated homes is the leading cause of lung cancer among non-smokers."
  },
  "why": "The physics doesn't do adjectives; it does numbers, and the numbers are measured per case."
